prompt: Load the kdevkit skill (from ~/.claude/skills/kdevkit/SKILL.md, ~/.kiro/steering/skills/kdevkit/SKILL.md, or ~/.codex/skills/kdevkit/SKILL.md — whichever exists). You are on branch feat/add-due-dates; the work is implemented and committed, and the user says: "ship it". Run the kdevkit closure phase: reconcile the feature spec's Implementation Plan (the work is done), then stage and make the closure commit. Do the git and file work now in this repo. When done print [kdevkit] applies. (Do not squash-merge or push — just reconcile and make the close commit.)
tools: claude,kiro,codex
--- setup ---
git init -q
git config user.email t@t.t && git config user.name t
git checkout -q -b feat/add-due-dates
mkdir -p specs/feature
cat > specs/feature/add-due-dates.md <<'MD'
# Feature: add-due-dates

## Feature Brief
Let a to-do carry a due date.

## Requirements
User can set and see a due date on any to-do.

## Design
A nullable due field on the record; a --due flag parses it.

## Implementation Plan
- [ ] add --due flag and parse the date
- [ ] render the due date in the list output

## Session Log

## Decision Log
MD
echo "fn main() {}" > code.rs
git add -A && git commit -q -m "feat: add due dates (implemented)"
--- assert ---
set -e
spec=specs/feature/add-due-dates.md
# Reconcile ticked the completed plan boxes — no unchecked boxes remain.
# (-- so grep doesn't read the "- [ ]" pattern as options.)
test -z "$(grep -F -- '- [ ]' "$spec" || true)"
grep -qF -- '- [x]' "$spec"
# A closure commit exists on top of the implementation commit.
git log --oneline | grep -qiE 'close\(|close:|closure'
# Closure does not move the spec out of feature/ (done in place).
test -f specs/feature/add-due-dates.md
